# Output=(MatrixElement,MO2ElectronIntegrals) Tran=(Full,Force)

probe_h2o_nowindow: the control. Identical to probe_h2o_rhf except that Window= is absent, so the transformation should cover all 7 MOs. This is the only way to prove Window= does anything: if this reports a 7^4 = 2401 two-electron block and probe_h2o_rhf reports 6^4 = 1296, the keyword works. If both come back the same size, Window= was silently ignored and the "never transform the full MO space" claim is false. Diff the two probe JSON reports; that comparison is this job's deliverable.

